  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nThe central idea is to solve the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem using a multilevel optimization strategy that combines binary and continuous representations. Unlike prior methods that focused on simple flips or continuous relaxations alone, this approach alternates between discrete binary states and interpolated continuous domains to escape local optima while maintaining a connection to the original objective. The key bottlenecks addressed include:\n- Limited exploration by pure binary search\n- Overly flat energy landscapes in continuous spaces\n- Balance between exploration and exploitation\nThe primary limitation is the complex gradient calculation required for continuous optimization, which we surmount by hybridizing with binary states and using surrogate models.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n- Binary variables: h_i \u2208 {0,1}\n- Outer function: f(h) = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n- Continuous surrogate: \u03b3(y) = max_k \u2225y * (1-y_k)\u2225_2 for y \u2208 [0,1]\n- Constraints: \u2211h_i = N/2, 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1\n- Derived variables: Binary projections onto continuous manifolds\n\nThe objective space is partitioned by:\n   1) Period-dominant configurations (length L<100)\n   2) Smooth interpolating structures (length N=380)\nEach subspace uses tailored optimization methods with explicit periodicity constraints.\n\nImplementation requires:\n- Fourier basis functions: \u03c6(x) = exp(2\u03c0i kx)\n- Gradient estimation: Monte Carlo surrogate gradients\n- Convexification: Power mean smoothing\n- Projection operators: Orthogonal hierarchies between binary/continuous spaces\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\na) Phase 1: Structured Initialization\n   - Generate periodic patterns using minimal phase quasiperiodic sequences\n   - Compute frequency spectra for each candidate\n   - Filter by energy constraint (C<0.381)\n\nb) Phase 2: Multi-Time Scale Annealing\n   - Primary moves: \n        - Block assembly (belt/brace method)\n        - Phase transition moves between dyadic representations\n        - Geometric morphing using IFS-like transformations\n   - Cooling schedule: T(i) = T0 * exp(-i/\u03bb) with \u03bb adapted from\n     $-\\ln(1-\\\\rho) \\approx 1.4e5$\n\nc) Phase 3: Continuous-Discrete Hierarchical Optimization\n   - Level 0: Raw binary bits\n   - Level 1: Binary strings as node graphs\n   - Level 2: Continuous embeddings via IDCT\n   - Transition: Exponential map between levels\n   - Metrics:msgap\u0302 = (h(x)\u2212h(x-k))\u00b7(\u2207h(x)+\u2207h(x-k))\n\nd) Exploration-Hexploitation Balance\n   - Period-based random walks of length p=4 to 8\n   - Energy stratification by Lyapunov exponent\n   - Physics-informed constraints:\n        \u2207\u00b7(p|\u2207f|) \u2264 \u03b4(x)\n        with \u03b4(x)~normal(\u03c3\u00b2)\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\na) Initial configurations:\n   - Mutilated Cantor dust (order 3)\n   - Thue-Morse concatenation\n   - Multifractal power spectra (\u03b1=0.7)\nb) Move topologies:\n   1. Local refinement: PBF (piecewise bowl flips)\n   2. Global reorganization: Fourier component resampling\n   3. Boundary moves: Exponential weighting of edge effects\nc) Adaptive scheduling:\n   - Mutation rate: r(i) = min(1, 1+0.5|log10(1-f(i))|)\n   - Step size adjustment: h_sigma(i) = \u03c3 * exp(\u03b2 i)\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\na) Phase allocations:\n   - Structured init: 10% budget (110s)\n   - Multi-scale annealing: 40% budget (440s)\n   - Continuous optimization: 40% budget (440s)\nb) Parallel jitter: 10% budget (110s)\nc) Failure detection:\n   - Abnormal termination: 1-sigma deviation from cooling curve\n   - Stalling: >10k consecutive states with \u0394E/svg <= 1e-6\nd) Budget monitoring: Explicit time checks every 50k evals\ne) Taxonomy-compliant restarts: \n   - 4\u00d7 exponential cooldown\n   - State reuse from previous scales via IFS maps\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\na) Feasibility checks:\n   1. Clipping: [0,1] exactly\n   2. Sum enforcement: mirror-biased adjustment (\u03bb=0.3)\n   3. Integer counts: exact N/2\nb) Score measurement:\n   - Direct comparison with Erd\u0151s convolution\n   - Resampling (5\u00d7) for noisy states\nc) Exception handling:\n   - Missing features: Zero padding with correlated noise\n   - Numerical overflow:\u27af Clustering adjustment\n   - Multiplicity alteration: Carte\u00e1n framework\nd) Output formatting:\n   - Enclosed within minimal_permutation operator\n   - Summary statistics: normalization_constant = 2/C\n   - Full disclosure: mode='full' correlation basis",
